{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310724,"nonce":"xFTxxZb26mLp8Bu1p4F+FHAhmRY=","title":"FIXED 2026-06-07. Root cause: forward-reference IrFunction stubs (1 block, 0 instructions, IrTerminator::Unreachable) for ...","message":"Per-token timing instrumentation was added to `GenerationLoop.generate`\nat the top of the function:\n\n```haxe\npublic function generate(prompt:String, onToken:Int-\u003eString-\u003eBool):String {\n    var rawEnv = Sys.getEnv(\"RAYZOR_TOKEN_TIMING\");  // \u003c-- this line\n    model.resetCache();\n    var ids = tokenizer.encode(prompt);\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nWith the env-read line present, decode hangs after `[gen] streaming...`\nprints from Main.hx but BEFORE any tokens are produced. No SIGILL,\nno panic — the program just sits silently. Without the line,\ndecode works normally at ~13 tok/s on the canonical Paris prompt.\n\n\nTested 7 variants in `GenerationLoop.generate`. Result table:\n\n| Variant | First statement | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| baseline | (none — original code) | works |\n| 1 | `Sys.getEnv(...)` + bool chain + Sys.println | hang |\n| 2 | `Sys.getEnv(...)` + var assignment | hang |\n| 3 | `var rawEnv = Sys.getEnv(...)` only | hang |\n| 4 | bare `Sys.getEnv(...);` statement | hang |\n| 5 | `Math.random();` (params:0, returns:F64) | **WORKS** |\n| 6 | `Sys.println(\"...\");` | prints, then hang |\n| 7 | `Sys.cpuTime();` (same shape as Sys.time) | hang |\n\nMath.random and Sys.time have **byte-identical mapping signatures**\nin `compiler/src/stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs`:\n- Math.random: `params: 0, returns: primitive, types: \u0026[] =\u003e F64`\n- Sys.time:    `params: 0, returns: primitive, types: \u0026[] =\u003e F64`\n\nYet one works and the other hangs.\n\n\nThe `generate` function ITSELF compiles to a real fn-ptr —\n`[fn-ptr] IrFunctionId(560002) nue.sampling.GenerationLoop.generate -\u003e\n0x10695e594` — and the entry-from-Main pathway runs (Main.hx's\n`[gen] streaming...` print appears). With Sys.println at the top of\ngenerate, the println actually fires (the print appears). So the\nSys call itself works at runtime.\n\nWhat hangs is whatever comes after — `tokenizer.encode` or\n`model.forwardIds` or `sampler.sample`. Those run fine in the\nbaseline. With a Sys call in the same function, they hang silently.\n\nNo `[trap-stub]` lines fire for any of the GenerationLoop functions.\nThe trap-stubs that DO appear\n(`haxe.iterators.ArrayKeyValueIterator.new`,\n`haxe.ds.TreeNode.new`, etc.) are present in BOTH the working and\nhung versions, so they don't explain the divergence.\n\n\nSame family as [[bugs-sys-getenv-in-ctor-residual]] which was\n\"resolved\" at 290e475 (branch-phi in lower_conditional_typed +\nper-block reaching-defs in scalar_replacement). That fix covered\nthe if/else-with-field-store-in-branches shape. This bug appears\nin a different shape:\n\n- `generate` is a METHOD, not a ctor\n- Function has a closure parameter (`Int-\u003eString-\u003eBool`)\n- First statement after the Sys call is an interface dispatch\n  (`model.resetCache()` where `model:CausalLanguageModel`)\n- The Sys call's result is unused\n\nThe combination of \"Sys-class call + interface dispatch on `this`\nin the next statement\" appears to be the trigger. Math-class calls\nin the same position do not trigger it.\n\n\n1. **Constructor-arg pattern** (the documented workaround from\n   [[bugs-sys-getenv-in-ctor-residual]]): read the Sys value in\n   `nue.Main.main` (where Sys works fine — Sys.time at Main.hx:352\n   has been working since 290e475) and thread it through\n   `new GenerationLoop(..., timingEnabled, ...)`. Inside generate,\n   read the constructor field; no Sys call inside the method body.\n\n2. **Move timing to Main.main's callback**: the streaming callback\n   `function(_id:Int, partial:String):Bool` runs in Main.main's\n   context. Time inside the callback, accumulating into a\n   `[Float]` array. Inside generate the loop calls onToken; from\n   the callback's perspective each call boundary IS a per-token\n   tick. This avoids any Sys call in GenerationLoop entirely.\n\n3. **Math.random()-based monotonic counter** if all you need is\n   relative ordering (e.g. \"is decode rate consistent vs\n   monotonic-decreasing\"): increment a counter, no clock. Doesn't\n   give absolute ms but answers the relative-rate question.\n\n4. **External instrumentation** via SIGPROF / `tools/profile_run.sh`\n   — already exists, doesn't require Haxe-side changes. Less\n   targeted but already works.\n\n\nThis bug deserves an isolated repro:\n\n1. Create a minimal Haxe class with one method matching the\n   shape: closure parameter + interface receiver + Sys call up\n   front + downstream method invocation.\n2. Build with `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1 RAYZOR_DUMP_CLIF=1` and diff\n   the emitted CLIF between the Sys.time and Math.random variants.\n3. Look for: (a) different extern symbol resolution, (b) a Sys-\n   class-specific egraph optimisation that mis-elaborates, (c) a\n   constant-fold that drops the call's required side-effect ordering.\n\nEstimated investigation: 1-2 sessions of focused compiler-internals\nwork. Not blocking — workarounds (1) and (2) are clean.\n\n\nThe minimal repro that hangs:\n```haxe\n// Inside GenerationLoop.generate at the top of the function body:\nMath.random();  // works\nSys.time();     // hangs\n```\n\nBuild, run llama-chat with any prompt, observe whether the model\nproduces any output past `[gen] streaming...`.\n\n\n- [[bugs-sys-getenv-in-ctor-residual]] — resolved at 290e475 for\n  the if/else field-store shape; this bug is in the same family\n  but a different code shape that the 290e475 fix doesn't cover\n- [[bugs-trap-stub-cascade]] — diagnostic infrastructure\n  (`RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1`) that produced the function-pointer\n  data confirming generate ITSELF compiles, the hang is in\n  downstream behaviour\n- [[project-compiler-ssa-hygiene-followups]] — the post-mortem\n  arc that produced the SROA + branch-phi fix line\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_sys_call_in_generation_method` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}